      "html" : "<\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-162363\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-162363\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>A potable ground water source or pump suction line shall not be located closer to potential sources of contamination than the distances shown in <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-162362', hash: '#JD_PCTable608.17.1' }}\">Table 608.17.1<\/Link>. In the event the underlying rock structure is limestone or fragmented shale, the local or state health department shall be consulted on well site location. The distances in <Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-162362', hash: '#JD_PCTable608.17.1' }}\">Table 608.17.1<\/Link> constitute minimum separation and shall be increased in areas of creviced rock or limestone, or where the direction of movement of the ground water is from sources of contamination toward the well.<\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-162364\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-162364\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><a name=\"JD_PCTable608.17.1\" id=\"JD_PCTable608.17.1\" title=\"PC Table 608.17.1\"><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Table 608.17.1<br><\/br>Distance from Contamination to Private Water Supplies and Pump Suction Lines<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-162365\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-162365\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>",
      "id" : "12274-html-1",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "A potable ground water source or pump suction line shall not be located closer to potential sources of contamination than the distances shown in Table 608.17.1 . In the event the underlying rock structure is limestone or fragmented shale, the local or state health department shall be consulted on well site location. The distances in Table 608.17.1 constitute minimum separation and shall be increased in areas of creviced rock or limestone, or where the direction of movement of the ground water is from sources of contamination toward the well.\n\n Table 608.17.1\n Distance from Contamination to Private Water Supplies and Pump Suction Lines"
    },
